A||N||2||superXmotorsports||removing engine from cradle||||4||
Z||000000||superXmotorsports||12-23-1999||06:23 PM||||Help!  I have 2 2.5/5spds in the cradle with the rear wheels and all attached sitting on the ground.  I need to seperate the engine from the cradle so my friend can come pick them up.  Is it possible to do this w/o an engine hoist?  Can I get to all the mounting bolts from the top?  I would appreciate any advice that can be given.  SXM.  <BR>**Monkeyman, no cutting torches!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||12-23-1999||09:16 PM||||Seperate all the motor mounts and exhaust. What's the big deal. You may had to unload the mounts to slide out a bolt or something but that's it. You can lift the thing like a sedan chair. put a 4x4 across the top and chain it to the lifting eyes.<P>If you take the tranny bolts, dust shield and starter off it will rest on the mounts till you move it, but you'll need to block the tranny so it doesn't fall. you'll be pulling the motor away from the tranny with the torque converter still on the flex plate.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||12-26-1999||08:41 PM||||C'mon, SuperX!  I would never suggest using a cutting torch.  A plasma cutter is much quicker! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
